    <h2>The 5 Items <em>Most Commonly Failed</em></h2>

    <div class="warning-box">
      <p><strong>Based on our 12,000+ cleans across Melbourne:</strong> These 5 items cause the most re-clean requests. Make sure these are spotless before your inspection.</p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>1. Oven interior</strong> — Built-up grease is the number one inspection fail across Melbourne. An oven that looks clean on the outside can still fail if the interior racks and base are not thoroughly degreased.</p>
    <p><strong>2. Shower screen</strong> — Soap scum and water mineral deposits build up on glass shower screens over time. A quick wipe is not enough — they need to be treated with a descaler and polished to streak-free clarity.</p>
    <p><strong>3. Rangehood filters</strong> — Agents specifically check rangehood filters for grease buildup. These need to be soaked and degreased, not just wiped.</p>
    <p><strong>4. Exhaust fans</strong> — Dust accumulates on exhaust fan covers in bathrooms and is a very common inspection flag. It takes 2 minutes to clean but is often missed.</p>
    <p><strong>5. Skirting boards</strong> — Agents run their finger along skirting boards. Dust and marks that accumulate over a tenancy must be fully removed.</p>

    <h2>What's <em>Not</em> on the Standard Checklist</h2>
    <p>The following items are not typically included in a standard end of lease clean and are usually quoted as extras:</p>
    <p>Full wall washing, blind washing, mould remediation, external windows above ground level, garage floors, and garden maintenance. Discuss these with your cleaning company before booking to get an accurate quote.</p>

